<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Truganini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1812–<a href="/years/1876">1876</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Truganini (c. 1812–1876), a Nuenonne woman from Bruny Island, guided George Augustus Robinson's expeditions in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-war">Black War</a> and was exiled with her people. She was wrongly called the last Aboriginal Tasmanian, a claim scholars and the Aboriginal Tasmanian community reject.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/truganini.jpg" alt="Truganini" width="330" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles A. Woolley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Truganini_-_Charles_Woolley_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
